        <h3><span class="mono text-secondary-content">Short bio · 50 words</span></h3>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[1.125rem] leading-relaxed text-pretty">Velvet Freight is a four-piece soul band from Duluth, Minnesota: Nora Halvorsen on voice and electric piano, Marcus Reyes on guitar, Tom Wierzbicki on bass and June Abernathy on drums. Since 2019 they have made five records of slow-burning soul played loud by a guitar band, the latest the album Breakwater (2026).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <h3><span class="mono text-secondary-content">Long bio · 250 words</span></h3>
        <div class="mt-5 max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-[1.125rem] leading-relaxed text-pretty">
          <p>Velvet Freight began in the winter of 2019, in a rehearsal room above a marine supply store on the Duluth harbor. Nora Halvorsen had been writing songs on a borrowed electric piano; Marcus Reyes answered her note on the store's bulletin board with a hollow-body guitar and a van; Tom Wierzbicki, who drove a city snowplow, came to the second rehearsal and stayed; June Abernathy, a Chicago drummer spending one summer up north, never went home.</p>
          <p>Their sound is soul taken slowly and played loud: a voice and a Rhodes up front, guitars that ring rather than shred, a rhythm section that waits for the song. They recorded the First Ice EP (2021) themselves on a four-track, then spent two years playing every room between Duluth and Thunder Bay before making their first album, Lake Effect (2023). Ore Dock Sessions (2025) caught two sold-out nights at the Harbor Room, with the snow coming sideways off the lake.</p>
          <p>Breakwater, their second album, came out in October 2026. Recorded live in nine days at Pier Nine Sound with producer Ada Lindqvist, without a click track, it is a record about staying put: about the people who keep the lights on at the end of the pier, and about choosing, every November, to see one more winter through. The band tours the Midwest and Ontario in February 2027 and plays Glasgow, Hamburg and Amsterdam in April.</p>
